    "created_at": "2024-01-15T12:38:24Z",
    "updated_at": "2024-01-15T12:38:24Z",
    "body": "> I wonder if we want an arbitrary extension point for this or just call into Trusted Types directly.\r\n\r\nI don't have a strong preference here. As long as it is possible to guard attribute mutations done by the DOM APIs, the actual algorithms can be defined in either spec. This PR was the only necessary [integration point of TT with DOM](https://w3c.github.io/trusted-types/dist/spec/#integration-with-dom). \r\n\r\nWhat might be problematic is not technical, i.e. can DOM call out to specs that are currently at FPWD? Waiting until CR is probably not very useful to the authors here, especially with shipped implementations.",
    "author_association": "NONE",
    "reactions": {
